<title>USA: Esquire to post charge after exec resigns.</title>
<headline>Esquire to post charge after exec resigns.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Esquire Communications Ltd said on Wednesday that David Feldman resigned his position as President and Chief Operating Officer for personal reasons.</p>
<p>Feldman will remain a member of Esquire's board of directors and act as a consultant to the company, Esquire said.</p>
<p>As a result of Feldman's resignation, the company anticipates recording a pre-tax charge of approximately $1.0 million in the second fiscal quarter of 1997, Esquire said.</p>
